# PIN-HOLD — the catalogue is deliberately behind upstream. Do not "catch it up".
#
# Read by scripts/verify-application-pin.sh --drift, which downgrades its alarm to a
# notice while this file names the currently-pinned tag. Delete the file when the hold
# ends; a hold naming a tag that is no longer pinned is reported as stale and loud.
#
# This exists because BEHIND is a true reading of a deliberate state, and the agent that
# reads it may be a fresh session after a restart with none of this context. A held pin
# that is only held in someone's head gets pinned away by the next person doing the
# obviously-right thing. That reader is not hypothetical: this agent has been restarted
# twice mid-programme, and the previous hold was released by its own stated condition
# rather than by anyone remembering — which is the whole point of writing one.

